---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import facsThumb from '../assets/tutorials/facs/2020-01-07-live-gate-facet-thumbnail.png';
import arcThumb from '../assets/tutorials/3c/2020-01-03-3c-arc-plot-1.png';

const tutorials = [
  {
    href: '/code/facs-with-r/',
    title: 'Analyzing high-throughput FACS assays with R',
    text: 'Traditional flow cytometry analysis software performs badly with large datasets. Here’s an example analysis workflow for a simple FACS-based assay run in 96-well format.',
    img: facsThumb,
    alt: 'Live-cell gate shown for every well of a 96-well plate',
  },
  {
    href: '/code/3c-arc-plot/',
    title: 'Plotting 3C data as arcs – a ggplot solution',
    text: '3C data measuring the interaction frequency between two genomic coordinates can be represented graphically as arcs between the anchor (aka viewpoint) and the region of interest. Here’s how to do this with ggplot.',
    img: arcThumb,
    alt: '3C arc plot',
  },
];
const hub = 'http://genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?db=hg38&position=chr3:187710000-188270000&hubUrl=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jchellmuth/BCL6.track.hub/master/hub.txt';
---
<Base title="Code" description="Code examples, tutorials and resources from the Hellmuth Lab, focusing on epigenetics, CRISPR and transcription factor biology.">
  <h1 class="section-title section-title--first">Posts &amp; Tutorials</h1>
  <ul class="tutorials">
    {tutorials.map((t) => (
      <li class="tutorial">
        <a href={t.href} class="tutorial__img"><Image src={t.img} alt={t.alt} widths={[320, 640]} sizes="(min-width: 40rem) 20rem, 100vw" /></a>
        <div>
          <h3><a href={t.href}>{t.title}</a></h3>
          <p>{t.text}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-title">Code and resources from published papers</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://www.cell.com/molecular-cell/fulltext/S1097-2765(20)30743-7" rel="noopener"><strong>Unique Immune Cell Coactivators Specify Locus Control Region Function and Cell Stage</strong></a><br />
    Chu and Hellmuth et al.<br />
    Mol Cell. 2020. PubMed PMID: <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33232656/" rel="noopener">33232656</a>
  </p>

  <h3>Resources</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>A <a href={hub} rel="noopener">UCSC track hub</a> to fully explore all relevant data at the <em>BCL6</em> locus.</li>
    <li>A version of this track hub <a href={`${hub}&highlight=hg38.chr3%3A187900071-187903310%230064C8%7Chg38.chr3%3A187918231-187920230%23808080%7Chg38.chr3%3A187934971-187936970%23808080%7Chg38.chr3%3A187941871-187947250%23808080%7Chg38.chr3%3A187957831-187959830%230064C8%7Chg38.chr3%3A187962431-187964430%23808080%7Chg38.chr3%3A187968751-187970750%230064C8%7Chg38.chr3%3A187973731-187975950%23808080%7Chg38.chr3%3A187977811-187980750%230064C8%7Chg38.chr3%3A187981291-187983290%23808080%7Chg38.chr3%3A187743727-187745726%23228B22`} rel="noopener">with highlights for each constituent enhancer</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Code</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>In silico design of a maximum-density CRISPR screening library – <a href="/resources/mol-cell-2020/1.1_Library-design-LCR.html">script 1.1</a></li>
    <li>Analysis of CRISPRi screening results
      <ul>
        <li>Screening data normalization and QC – <a href="/resources/mol-cell-2020/2.1_CRISPRi-analysis.html">script 2.1</a></li>
        <li>Identification of essential enhancers – <a href="/resources/mol-cell-2020/2.2_enhancer_definition.html">script 2.2</a></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>R-based FACS analysis for drop-out experiments – <a href="/code/facs-with-r/">tutorial</a></li>
    <li>Transcription factor motif analysis
      <ul>
        <li>Motif download, processing and matching to a region of interest (<em>BCL6</em> locus) – <a href="/resources/mol-cell-2020/3.1_TF-motif-matching.html">script 3.1</a></li>
        <li>Motif density comparison in essential vs non-essential enhancers – <a href="/resources/mol-cell-2020/3.2_TF-motif-density.html">script 3.2</a></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>

</Base>
